# Dual 16 GB VRAM GPU — vLLM (2× RTX 5060 Ti 16GB = 32 GB total, tp=2, Blackwell)
#
# RUNNING since 2026-09-23 (second card fitted). Results per entry below; serving-side tuning and
# multi-agent numbers: ~/GIT/llm-service-provider/upgrade-dual-5060.md, Steps 6-7.
# Companion to models/16gb.vllm (single-card smoke tests). Steps: test-plan-5060ti.md, Part B.
#
# The second card goes in via PCIe bifurcation, so each card likely runs at x8. tp=2 sends
# an all-reduce over PCIe for every layer of every token, so link width is a real speed
# factor (on the 4090 rig, AWQ tp=2 ran 16.6 tok/s vs 28.5 tok/s at tp=1). Check with:
#   nvidia-smi --query-gpu=index,pcie.link.gen.current,pcie.link.width.current --format=csv
#
# Don't run fetch-hf.sh on this file (see the format note in models/16gb.vllm):
#   - HF-format entries (gguf-file "-") download themselves on the first `vllm serve`.
#   - The 32B GGUF comes via: ./fetch-hf.sh models/candidates.txt --models qwen2.5-coder:32b-q4
#
# Operational steps for the whole upgrade (hardware checks, the serving-side switch to tp=2, how many
# users it serves, DDR5 sizing, rollback): ~/GIT/llm-service-provider/upgrade-dual-5060.md
#
# Run once the second card is in (./gpu-mode.sh multi first):
#   VLLM_BIN=~/vllm-env/bin/vllm ./run.sh --backend vllm --model-file models/2x16gb.vllm \
#     --models qwen3.8-27b:nvfp4

# ── Primary target: Qwen3.8-27B, NVFP4, native Blackwell tensor-core path ────
# Same dense Gated-DeltaNet-hybrid architecture as this repo's own extensively
# tested qwen3.8:27b (llama-server Q4_K_M, f16 KV — see 24gb.txt/2x24gb.txt/
# 3x24gb.txt and the python_hashmap precision-canary notes in CLAUDE.md).
# RTX 5060 Ti is Blackwell (sm_120) with native NVFP4 tensor cores.
# Two vLLM main commits help this exact combo and are NOT in the 0.29.0 release:
# 13cf9e05c1 (prefer W4A4 NVFP4 linear kernels on SM120/121) and f6326f53bd (FlashInfer
# Gated DeltaNet prefill kernel on SM12x). Install vLLM from main.
#
# VERIFIED 2026-09-15 on the HF Hub: repo exists, 19 files, 20.6 GB, includes
# tokenizer.json. config.json: Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration (model_type qwen3_5),
# compressed-tensors "nvfp4-pack-quantized", 4-bit weights AND 4-bit activations
# (group size 16, fp8 scales), bf16 base, max_position_embeddings 262144. It ships
# preprocessor/video configs, so the vision tower is in there too (unused for text).
# Still unverified: output quality. Web research for this pick was noisy (several
# differently-named "Qwen3.8-27B NVFP4" repos claiming 14-23 GB), and 4-bit
# activations are a real precision risk for python_hashmap — watch that task.
#
# RESULTS on 2x RTX 5060 Ti (2026-09-23/24): python_hashmap PASS; spot 9/10 at 30.0 tok/s on vLLM
# 569adb5a97 with enforce_eager (W4A16 kernel; node_paratrooper the only fail). This entry is kept
# as that baseline; the tuned serving config is `qwen3.8-27b:nvfp4-next` below (10/10 spot).
# enforce_eager was a first-run precaution; CUDA graphs are fine on this model (Step 6 of
# ~/GIT/llm-service-provider/upgrade-dual-5060.md). kv_cache_dtype intentionally NOT set to fp8: qwen3.6:27b/qwen3.8:27b need
# f16-equivalent KV precision or python_hashmap silently drops the `_EMPTY` sentinel
# (see CLAUDE.md's python_hashmap precision-canary section).
qwen3.8-27b:nvfp4  -  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=32768,enforce_eager,enable_prefix_caching  hf:QUASAR-QAT/Qwen3.8-27B-QUASAR-NVFP4

# ── Fallbacks: Qwen2.5-Coder-32B, the strongest coder on this repo's llama-server benchmark ──
# (PERFECT 19/19 coding.) KV sizing: ~256 KB/token at fp16 (64 layers, 8 KV heads, dim 128),
# i.e. ~128 KB/token per card at tp=2. Each card holds ~9.7 GB of weights plus ~3.5 GB of vLLM
# overhead (measured on one 5060 Ti with the 14B, 2026-09-15), leaving ~1.5 GiB of KV per card at
# 0.92: 8192 tokens (~1 GiB per card) fits, 16384 doesn't. vLLM prints the real limit.
# Not 0.95: Windows holds ~1.1 GiB of the display card (invisible to nvidia-smi in WSL), so
# only 0.929 is free there, and tp=2 applies one utilization value to both cards.
# AWQ first: stock vLLM, no plugin. Verified 2026-09-15: 19.3 GB, ships a tokenizer.
qwen2.5-coder:32b-awq  -  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=8192,gpu_mem_util=0.92,enable_prefix_caching  hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct-AWQ
# GGUF via vllm-gguf-plugin. GGUF from bartowski via models/candidates.txt; hf: is the tokenizer repo.
qwen2.5-coder:32b-5060ti  Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=8192,gpu_mem_util=0.92,enable_prefix_caching  hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct

# Step-6 tuning of the serving lane (2026-09-24): CUDA graphs on (no enforce_eager) and the CUTLASS
# W4A4 kernel forced. vLLM builds before 13cf9e05c1 (2026-09-08) auto-pick FlashInferCuteDslNvFp4W4A16
# (bf16 activations) on sm_120; `cutlass` runs activations in FP4 too — ~2x prefill, the precision
# risk python_hashmap watches. RESULT (569adb5a97): hashmap PASS x2, spot 9/10 at 32.8 tok/s, 330.8 s.
# language_model_only + max_num_seqs=4: without them startup OOMs (vision profiling, 256 slots).
qwen3.8-27b:nvfp4-w4a4  -  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=32768,linear_backend=cutlass,language_model_only,max_num_seqs=4,enable_prefix_caching  hf:QUASAR-QAT/Qwen3.8-27B-QUASAR-NVFP4
# Same, on vLLM >= bbd7c24d6e (has 13cf9e05c1 + f6326f53bd, FlashInfer 0.7.0): no linear_backend
# needed — auto picks FlashInferCutlassNvFp4 (W4A4) and the FlashInfer GDN prefill kernel on sm_120.
# RESULT 2026-09-24 (VLLM_BIN=~/vllm-env-next/bin/vllm, bbd7c24d6e): spot 10/10 at 32.6 tok/s,
# 354.3 s — node_paratrooper PASS (134 s, one run); python_hashmap PASS x2.
# FULL RUN 2026-09-24: coding 19/19 (dotnet_sas needs .NET 9 — this Ubuntu has 8 system-wide, 9 in
# ~/.dotnet), web 4/4, L6 stepped 4/4, node_paratrooper 1/7 over all runs (a rare pass),
# ~32-33 tok/s. Context/multihop: the -128k entry below.
# This is the configuration the llm-service-provider lane serves.
qwen3.8-27b:nvfp4-next  -  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=32768,language_model_only,max_num_seqs=4,enable_prefix_caching  hf:QUASAR-QAT/Qwen3.8-27B-QUASAR-NVFP4
# Context/multihop variant of the above: 131072 cap (the ~140k-token KV pool holds one 128k
# request; context_256k is skipped by its min_vram_gb guard and this cap).
# RESULT 2026-09-24: context 8k-128k 5/5 (context_128k 71 s), multihop 5/5, context_256k skipped.
qwen3.8-27b:nvfp4-next-128k  -  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=131072,language_model_only,max_num_seqs=4,enable_prefix_caching  hf:QUASAR-QAT/Qwen3.8-27B-QUASAR-NVFP4
